        "message": "LU-6132 o2iblnd: release the pools of an old HCA\n\nA failover replaces the hdev of a dev and fails each pool on the old\nhdev. A failed pool that is in use goes to ps_failed_pool_list.\nOnly the net shutdown frees it. So the old hdev stays until the net\ngoes. A pool that o2iblnd creates during the swap can also\nkeep the old hdev.\n\nFree a failed pool when its last node or map returns. Add\nibd_hdev_gen. Destroy a new pool if the HCA changes while o2iblnd\ncreates it. Map and unmap a tx on the HCA of its pool.\n\nWith dev_failover=2, the failover thread replaces the hdev about\nevery 10 s, so this path runs without bonding.\n\nFixes: 7b442f1a4371 (\"b=20153 add IB bonding failover support to o2iblnd\")\nFixes: 94d1ce46562b (\"LU-7101 lnet: per NI map-on-demand value\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial nettype=o2ib testlist=sanity-lnet\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I55255cf3aaf510ce66737eaf991cb5204d3ea288\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
